A lease of immoveable property determines—
(a) by efflux of the time limited thereby;
(e) by express surrender;
(f) by implied surrender;
(g) by forfeiture; that is to say, (1) in case the lessee breaks an express condition which provides that, on breach thereof, the lessor may re-enter...; or (2) in case the lessee renounces his character as such by setting up a title in a third person...;
(h) on the expiration of a notice to determine the lease, or to quit... duly given by one party to the other.
